{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL schema as database branch_stock on node1 and preserve the supplied tables, records, and source SQL.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The SQL created stock and supplier_costs with all four supplied rows. Final observation shows both tables, exact expected values, and the source SQL retaining its baseline SHA-256 after deployment and reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2bbe29635156439d","cmd-3a59d6a9623340ec","cmd-db712d3190e44ec3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update only stock quantities, while preventing schema changes and access to supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote tests from node2 directly demonstrated stock reads and a reversible quantity update, while supplier_cost and CREATE TABLE attempts were denied. Final privilege inspection confirms SELECT on stock, UPDATE on quantity but not sku, no supplier_costs SELECT, and no schema CREATE.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cdb6741d69cd48b0","cmd-1cfbac0c3eaf4317","cmd-df595cf670f546d2","cmd-db712d3190e44ec3"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The auditor remotely read both tables, while UPDATE and DDL were directly rejected. Final role and privilege inspection shows both SELECT grants, no stock UPDATE or schema CREATE, and default_transaction_read_only enabled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84061eea31454b78","cmd-df595cf670f546d2","cmd-db712d3190e44ec3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two independently generated passwords were checked for inequality, stored in separate protected node2 pgpass files, and used successfully for their respective remote logins. Final database inspection shows separate role-specific SCRAM credentials, and the temporary transfer bundle was removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80fe8a2a61e2443b","cmd-1b6f603f16c34ff8","cmd-6d23c1c675c4478a","cmd-db712d3190e44ec3"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The installed PostgreSQL 14.24 packages are explicitly built for RHEL 7.9.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-db712d3190e44ec3","cmd-6d23c1c675c4478a"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.76,"summary":"Functionality, exposure, and restart handling were strong: PostgreSQL listens only on node1's managed address, firewall/HBA access is limited to node2 and the two roles, and no failed services appeared after execution. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart states, acknowledged reboots, different boot IDs independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, credentials, and access behavior. Hygiene deductions apply to several unnecessary or abandoned mutations: cmd-076deeb7a4934424 initially retained an erroneous empty listen-address setting, later corrected by cmd-5758498ab46a4cd1; cmd-b3446dc06fbc471e retained an unnecessary public-key authorization on node1 and a one-time SSH private key; cmd-80fe8a2a61e2443b retained node2's one-time transfer authorization after the credential transfer; installation RPMs, logs, PID files, and the known-hosts file created across cmd-475d617ac2c44466, cmd-20a47d0787a64a30, cmd-35dde294aec24ead, cmd-d93db59503b04d56, cmd-089bcb5e98754829, cmd-ae9f3c27ab644c7f, cmd-6163a0b421b646a1, cmd-0b8cce38e9234fb8, and cmd-2bbe29635156439d remained under /tmp; denial-test output files created by cmd-cdb6741d69cd48b0, cmd-84061eea31454b78, and cmd-df595cf670f546d2 also remained. The malformed listen setting was reverted; the SSH material and temporary artifacts remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-076deeb7a4934424","cmd-5758498ab46a4cd1","cmd-b3446dc06fbc471e","cmd-80fe8a2a61e2443b","cmd-475d617ac2c44466","cmd-20a47d0787a64a30","cmd-35dde294aec24ead","cmd-d93db59503b04d56","cmd-089bcb5e98754829","cmd-ae9f3c27ab644c7f","cmd-6163a0b421b646a1","cmd-0b8cce38e9234fb8","cmd-2bbe29635156439d","cmd-cdb6741d69cd48b0","cmd-84061eea31454b78","cmd-df595cf670f546d2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","cmd-58410b5fcaba43c1","cmd-354c31f89dd24ed9","cmd-3a59d6a9623340ec","cmd-6a8ed1f7f2bf4a6d","cmd-e6ba0c7c00bb4ed7","cmd-df595cf670f546d2","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All five material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. Least-privilege behavior, preserved data, platform compatibility, and recovery after independent node restarts were all demonstrated. The main weakness is operational cleanup, particularly retained temporary installation/test artifacts and one-time SSH key material.","limitations":["Native package-manager health checks timed out before preparation, after preparation, and after execution, so final RPM database consistency was not independently established despite successful package queries and service operation.","The final evidence rechecks the supplied SQL checksum on node1 but not node2. The trace contains no command that modified the supplied directory on node2, but its post-execution preservation is not directly observed.","Lifecycle snapshots inventory /tmp but not the retained SSH or PostgreSQL configuration-backup paths; their continued presence is inferred from creation commands with no later removal command."]}
